# Nanfu kernel patch series.
#
# Every entry is a patch against the pinned upstream tag named by
# Nanfu-Patch-Applies-To in the patch's own header (currently 155.0.8059.85).
# Order matters: entries apply top to bottom, and a patch sees the tree as the
# entries above it left it. A patch that needs a file another patch creates
# goes after it.
#
# Constraints, checked by kernel/verify-patches.sh and enforced in review:
#   - every patches/NNNN-*.patch file is listed here exactly once;
#   - numbers are never reused, and a dropped patch leaves a gap on purpose;
#   - entries otherwise ascend by number.
#
# Files under patches/examples/ are illustrations and are never listed here.
# The order below is the list in kernel/pinned.json, which is authoritative.
#
# Format notes and the lifecycle of a patch: kernel/patches/README.md.

0001-add-webgl-vendor-renderer-switches.patch
0002-add-client-rects-jitter-seed.patch
0003-tls-enable-server-handshake-padding.patch
